# RAG Vector Store

Reusable guidelines for ticket RAG indexing and retrieval. Apply them when designing or changing vector-store, embedding, or grounded-answer code.

## Chunking

- One knowledge document per ticket section: description, each comment, resolution notes.
- Split paragraph-based; max ~800 tokens per chunk.
- Use ~100 token overlap only when a single section must be split.

## Metadata

- Every chunk carries: `ticketId`, `status`, `priority`, `assignee`, `category`, `sourceType`.

## Embedding

- Use Ollama `nomic-embed-text` (local, 768 dimensions).
- Model choice and rationale live in `specs/architecture.md`.

## Retrieval configuration

- Read `topK` and `similarityThreshold` from `application.yml`.
- Never hardcode retrieval thresholds in code.

## Re-ingestion

- On ticket create, update, comment, or status change: delete all chunks for that `ticketId`, then index new ones.

## Grounding

- Answer only from retrieved context; cite ticket IDs in responses.
- When retrieval is empty, return an explicit "No relevant tickets found" and skip the LLM call.
- Use a single retrieve-then-generate flow; no agentic actions.

## Prompting

- Keep the static system prompt as a constant prefix for prompt-caching compatibility.
